/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/deployments","created_at":"2014-01-31T13:39:22Z","updated_at":"2025-12-13T09:22:08Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-13T05:17:45Z","git_url":"git://github.com/neovim/neovim.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:neovim/neovim.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/neovim/neovim.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/neovim/neovim","homepage":"https://neovim.io","size":355316,"stargazers_count":94890,"watchers_count":94890,"language":"Vim Script","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":6465,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":2020,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["api","c","lua","neovim","nvim","text-editor","vim"],"visibility":"public","forks":6465,"open_issues":2020,"watchers":94890,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"### Neovim version (nvim -v)\r\n\r\nNVIM v0.7.0-dev+737-g818ae74ea\r\n\r\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\r\n\r\nidk\r\n\r\n### Operating system/version\r\n\r\n5.10.70-1-MANJARO\r\n\r\n### Terminal name/version\r\n\r\nxfce4-terminal\r\n\r\n### $TERM environment variable\r\n\r\nxterm-256color\r\n\r\n### Installation\r\n\r\nAUR\r\n\r\n### How to reproduce the issue\r\n\r\n#### Script\r\nThe following script is used to create a simple popup window. Save the script to somewhere in your local file system.\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal api = vim.api\r\n\r\nlocal function create_temp_buf()\r\n  local buf = api.nvim_create_buf(false, true) -- create new emtpy buffer\r\n  return buf\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal function create_popup_win(buf)\r\n  -- get dimensions\r\n  local width = api.nvim_get_option(\"columns\")\r\n  local height = api.nvim_get_option(\"lines\")\r\n\r\n  -- calculate our floating window size\r\n  local win_height = math.ceil(height * 0.5 - 4)\r\n  local win_width = math.ceil(width * 0.5)\r\n\r\n  -- and its starting position\r\n  local row = math.ceil((height - win_height) / 2 - 1)\r\n  local col = math.ceil((width - win_width) / 2)\r\n\r\n  -- set some options\r\n  local opts = {\r\n    style = \"minimal\",\r\n    relative = \"editor\",\r\n    width = win_width,\r\n    height = win_height,\r\n    row = row,\r\n    col = col,\r\n    border = 'single',\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  -- and finally create it with buffer attached\r\n  win = api.nvim_open_win(buf, true, opts)\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal buf, win\r\n\r\nlocal function open_window()\r\n  buf = create_temp_buf()\r\n  win = create_popup_win(buf)\r\nend\r\n\r\nopen_window()\r\n```\r\n\r\n#### Reproduciable Steps\r\n- Start pure nvim: `/usr/bin/nvim --clean`\r\n- Open a floating window by sourcing the simple popup window script.\r\n- Run a terminal with fzf command inside the floating window by executing `:terminal fzf --reverse --height 80\\%`\r\n\r\n  (to keep fzf program busy, you can `:lcd` to a directory with a large number of files)\r\n\r\n- During fzf continuing searching files, exit the floating window by fisrt pressing `<C-\\><C-n>` then executing `:q`\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nThe popup window exits without any error.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nThe nvim program crashes with message `fish: Job 1, '/usr/bin/nvim --clean' terminated by signal SIGSEGV (Address boundary error)`\r\n  ![https://i.imgur.com/lysH6wS.gif](https://i.imgur.com/lysH6wS.gif)\r\n\r\n### Additional Info\r\nTried removing one of the `--reverse` and `--height 80%` options for fzf and after that no segmentation fault happened.\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/16699/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/16699/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]